{"tool_name":"graphgr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"graphgr","home":"https://github.com/pulimeng/GraphGR","summary":"A graph neural network to predict the effect of pharmacotherapy on the cancer cell growth.\n\nGraphGR is a tool to predict drug (kinase inhibitors ONLY for now) response on a specific cell line given genetic information of the cell line, binding affinity of the drug to the proteins, and the disease association scores of the proteins. It utilizes heterogeneous data to construct a graph for each cell-line-drug combination (instance). The trained model can be used to predict the effect (currently a binary classification) of a drug on a given cell line.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T08:58:05Z","last_update_date":"2021-01-25T09:46:18Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:graphgr","credit":[{"email":"michal@brylinski.org","name":"Michal Brylinski","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Text mining","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0306"},{"term":"Virtual screening","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3938"}]}],"name":"GraphGR","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.05.20.107458"}],"topic":[{"term":"Epigenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3173"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Oncology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2640"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"GraphGR","home":"https://bio.tools/graphgr","summary":"A graph neural network to predict the effect of pharmacotherapy on the cancer cell growth.\n\nGraphGR is a tool to predict drug (kinase inhibitors ONLY for now) response on a sp